window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["vw/tiguan-5n"]={"tiguan-5n-activate-bluetooth-on-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth on the RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION: Not all RNS-315 are equipped with a Bluetooth module.</strong> </p>\n<figure><table><thead><tr><td>Module compatibility list</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3C0 035 279</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 A</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 B</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 C</td><td>Yes (conditional)</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 D</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 E</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 F</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 G</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 H</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 J</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 K</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>You can also remove the RNS 315 from its slot to check. Behind it, you’ll find a label with the RNS-315’s MAC address.<br/>If the MAC address contains only zeros (MAC: 00:00:00:00:00:00), your RNS-315 is not equipped with the Bluetooth module. </p>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns_315_j_mac_non-6328b9e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns315_mac_oui-eed1a386.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>3</strong><br/>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Uncheck the “Telephone Transceiver inactive” box</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS315_3C0-035-279_Module37_Byte3-74e93c9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-activate-hidden-menu-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the hidden menu in RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Developer mode (temporary)</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong><em>Enabled</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart RNS 315.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-035-279_Module37_Adaptation_Developer_mode_tem-59109da4.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-activate-hidden-menu-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the hidden menu in RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>56 – Radio</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 50</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1T0-035-680-C_Module37_Adaptation_Channel50-1a7d6a90.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-activate-rns-510-voice-command":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate voice control on the RNS 510 (SDS).  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:</strong> RNS 510 firmware must be version v2660.</p>\n<p>Activating voice control brings up the “Voice control” menu in the RNS 510’s SETUP menu.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>3</strong>, check the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Microphone Diagnostics active</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>7</strong>, uncheck the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Voice Control inactive</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS510_Menu_Commande_Vocale-bf5955d7.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>To install the microphone, connect the microphone lead to the rear of the RNS 510. Connect to pins (Mic-)C1 and (Mic+)C7. </p>","tiguan-5n-activate-turn-signals-in-us-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the US turn signals. (Tiguan 5N Phase 1 only)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>Byte 7</strong>: Enter the value<strong> 32</strong> in the ” <strong>Dec</strong>” field<br/>” (brightness value in %, origin: 0)</p>\n<p>Decimal examples shown in yellow in the image:<br/>14 (corresponds to a 20% variation in the indicator lights)<br/>1E (corresponds to a 30% variation in the indicator lights)<br/>28 (corresponds to a 40% variation in the indicator lights)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-937-049-Q_Module09_Byte7-16502f21.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-corner-lights-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activating the <strong>cornering lights</strong> causes the fog light on the side toward which you’re turning the steering wheel to turn on when traveling at speeds below 50 km/h. This feature is also called “cornering lights.” Once this feature is activated on your Tiguan, the fog light on the side of the turn you’re making will turn on! It’s super handy on narrow roads or in roundabouts.     </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>23</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Internal Turn Light Control Algorithm active”</em><br/><em>Bits <strong>3–4</strong>: Select “08 Turn Lights via fog lights” from the drop-down list</em></p>","tiguan-5n-ambient-lighting-intensity":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Used to adjust ambient lighting intensity. And activate it for retrofit. (floor lighting) For phase 1.    </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>” then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 05</strong> (Footwell Lightning Dimming)  </p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select intensity from 20 to 100% (in 1% increments)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>If your lighting is not activated or after retrofit installation<em>.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em>Set <em>Bit <strong>7</strong> </em> </p>","tiguan-5n-automatic-closing-of-windows-and-roof-in-the-event-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Automatically closes the windows and sunroof when it rains. </p>\n<p>The vehicle must be locked using the remote control for this to work. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf561-c90da3e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “2” and click ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf56-9439cbb9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte <strong>0 and </strong>check bit<strong> 2</strong>, <strong>“Rain Closing active</strong>,” to enable the windows and roof to close when it rains:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-5-d61c5dd9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>7 – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu</p>\n<p> Then click “OK”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-7-353fb01b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click <strong>“46 – Comfort Module”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Then click <strong>” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “</strong></p>\n<p><em><strong>6</strong> – Select Byte <strong>9</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Rain Closing (0 = nonrecurring / 1 = permanent)” </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 2</strong>: Uncheck “Comfort Closing via Rain Light Sensor (Rain Closing) inactive” </em> </p>","tiguan-5n-automatic-door-locking":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set automatic door locking from 15km/h.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres_vw-auto-loc-ce03b1da.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Auto-Lock (automatic locking from 15 km/h)”. </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-automatic-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set automatic door unlocking when the ignition key is removed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Canal 05</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set value to 1</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw-door-unlock-798a1163.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3 : </strong> Check “Auto-Unlock (unlocking after removing key from ignition)”. </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-automatic-headlamp-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte 0 Bit 0: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-automatic-headlamp-activation-in-the-event-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>1: </strong> Check “Rain Light Function Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-changing-the-image-of-the-rcd-rns-ops":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the vehicle image of the OPS (parking aid) on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Encoding 07</strong>,” then ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose Byte<strong> 6</strong> or <strong>9</strong></p>\n<p><em><em>Select</em>the vehicle <em>from the drop-down menu</em>:</em><br/><br/>00 = via CAN<br/>01 = Polo 6R<br/>02 = New Beetle<br/>03 = New Beetle Cabrio<br/>04 = Scirocco<br/>05 = Golf 5<br/>06 = Jetta<br/>07 = Golf 6 Variant<br/>08 = Golf 6 Cabrio<br/>09 = Touran<br/>0A = Golf Plus<br/>0C = Tiguan<br/>0D = Sharan<br/>0E = EOS<br/>0F = Passat 3C<br/>10 = Passat Limousine<br/>11 = Passat Variant<br/>13 = Caddy<br/>14 = T5<br/>2C = Skoda Octavia<br/>2D = Skoda Octavia Kombi<br/>2E = Skoda Superb Kombi</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_0864-978ed9ed.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD or RNS must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","tiguan-5n-changing-the-rcd-rns-510-theme":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the display theme of the RCD 510 and RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” for RNS510 and “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” for RCD510.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>4-5</strong>: Select from 3 themes</em><br/><em>“00 Display Variant: Highline</em><br/><em>“10 Display Variant: Sportsline</em><br/><em>“20 Display Variant: Premium</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/69C76009-6EC7-465A-A676-8E39BA840A6B-6689b9e0.webp\"/><figcaption>Highline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3A58F148-9FBB-4DD8-BF05-E03A5351E3A8-e9b6cb9b.webp\"/><figcaption>Sportsline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4894A3B7-2ED2-4A75-9D46-CA3BFCF5A76C-8fb8de15.webp\"/><figcaption>Premium</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD / RNS 510 must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","tiguan-5n-comfort-blinker":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select<strong>“Comfort Turn Signal”</strong> from the drop-down list </p>\n<p>Choose a value between 1 and 5 for the number of flashes</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/confortturnsignalg6-6da68fad.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><em>Note: If you have a post-2011 Tiguan and the flash count has not changed after coding, you may need to activate the option in the MFA+ ODB.<br/>In Options, go to Settings, then Lighting, Factory settings, then tick Factory settings and select OK.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/golf6-turn-signal-blinks-e68241dd.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-coming-home-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is locked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01</strong> (Coming-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>","tiguan-5n-deactivate-brake-pad-warning-light":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to disable the brake pad wear warning light on the OBD (On-Board Diagnostics) system, for example, for brake pads without a sensor or if the sensor is malfunctioning / Brake Pad Warning Light Deactivation. </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>17 – Instruments</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong>Click on <strong>“Coding –</strong> 07”  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> <em>–  <em>The third and fourth digits of the code (xx<strong>??</strong>x0x) are used to change the settings for the Instrument module. To turn off the brake pad warning light, subtract <strong>01</strong> from these digits. </em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instruments-Coding-Golf5-2c5d8d07.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In the example above, the initial code is: <strong>0027103</strong></p>\n<p>To turn off the brake pad warning light, simply recode it as follows: <strong>0026103 </strong><em>(27 – 01 = 26)</em></p>\n<p>To turn on the brake pad warning light: +01</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant-frein-d4619ec9.gif\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-deactivate-rear-wiper-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate automatic activation of the rear windshield wiper during reversing when the front windshield wipers are operating.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em><strong>Byte 1 :</strong></em><br/><em><strong>Bit 7 </strong>: Uncheck “Rear Wiper with Front Wiper continiously active”.</em></p>\n<p><em><strong>Byte 2 : </strong></em><br/><em><strong>Bit 0</strong>: Uncheck “Rear Wiper with Front Wiper intermitent active”.</em></p>","tiguan-5n-deactivate-windshield-washer-indicator":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> <em>–  <em>The third and fourth coding digits (xx<strong>??</strong>x0x) are used to modify Instrument module options. To remove the ice-washer indicator, subtract <strong>04</strong> from these digits. </em></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instruments-Coding-Golf5-2c5d8d07.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In the example above, the initial coding is: <strong>0027103</strong></p>\n<p>To remove the windscreen washer indicator, simply recode as follows: <strong>0023103 </strong><em>(27 – 04 = 23)</em></p>\n<p>To activate the ice washer indicator: +04</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglace-edc83d4f.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-deactivate-activate-electric-handbrake-for-rear-brake-pad-change":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate/activate the electric handbrake in maintenance mode in order to change/replace the rear brake pad/disc linings. (EPB reset / Lining change mode)  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/>To start, set the gear lever to P, remove the electric handbrake on the button and preferably connect a battery charger according to the vehicle manual. Check that there are no faults/errors before starting basic setup.<br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“53 – Parking Brake</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Basic setting</strong> <strong>– 04</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Channel <strong>007</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Click on<strong>“Go</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Basic Settings: <strong>OFF</strong> during the procedure, then <strong>ON</strong> when finished (yellow arrow).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/53epb007-8e9a2db6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>A fault message will appear on your ODB indicating<strong>“Parking brake fault</strong>” and an LED in the parking brake switch, but this is normal and should be ignored.<br/><br/> 7 – Once finished, go back (Done, Go Back) until the program closes.<br/><br/> 8 – Switch off the vehicle’s ignition, then disconnect the VAG-COM cable<br/><br/> 9 – <strong>Change the linings on both sides!</strong><br/><br/><br/></p>\n<p><strong>To reactivate the electric handbrake :</strong><br/><br/><br/><strong>10</strong> – With engine off and ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>11</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>12</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“53 – Parking Brake</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>13</strong> – Click on<strong>“Basic setting – 04</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>14</strong> – Select Channel <strong>006</strong><br/><br/><strong>15</strong> – Click on<strong>“Go</strong>”.<br/><br/>Basic Settings: <strong>OFF</strong> during the procedure, then <strong>ON </strong>when finished (yellow arrow).</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/53epb006-52154901.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>16</strong> – Once finished, go back (Done, Go Back) until the program is closed.</p>\n<p><strong>17</strong> – Switch off the ignition and disconnect the VAG-COM cable.</p>","tiguan-5n-defrost-time-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the operating time for mirror and rear window defrosting.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong> then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong> (Rear Window &amp; Outside Mirror Heater Activation Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>1 to 254 min</strong> (in 1 min increments).</p>","tiguan-5n-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> –  <em>The third and fourth coding digits (xx<strong>??</strong>x0x) are used to modify Instrument module options. To suppress the belt alarm, subtract <strong>2</strong> from these digits. </em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/17-Instruments-Coding-Golf5-2c5d8d07.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>In the example above, the initial coding (with belt alarm) is: <strong>0023103</strong></p>\n<p>To delete the belt alarm, simply recode as follows: <strong>0021103 </strong><em>(23 – 02 = 21)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-disable-license-plate-illumination-odb-led-error":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Disables license plate light control. Useful when installing LED bulbs without resistance or for error prevention.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>23</strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Uncheck: “Lamp Monitoring (Cold) License Plate Lamps Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/led_plaque5-odt_147-d36567c5.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-door-lock-confirmation-key":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the door lock confirmation when using the key.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>Channel 11</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: </strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0: </strong> Check “Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks” (confirmation with blinking lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks” (confirmation with a beep or horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/locking_196-096e4b1a.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-door-lock-confirmation-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the door lock confirmation when using the remote control. </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 10</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vagcom-golf5-e5c80be6.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2: </strong> Check “Locking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control” (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control” (confirmation with a beep or horn)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/locking_196-096e4b1a.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-door-unlock-confirmation-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to set the door unlock confirmation when using the remote control.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 07</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>10</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 2</strong>: Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Remote Control” (confirmation with flashing lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Tick “Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Remote Control” (confirmation with Beep/Horn)</em></p>","tiguan-5n-door-unlocking-confirmation-key":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the door unlock confirmation when using the key.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>Channel 08</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to 0 (no confirmation)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 1 (confirmation with turn signals)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 2 (confirmation with beep/horn)</em><br/><em>Set the value to 3 (confirmation with turn signals and a beep/horn)</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>10</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Blink) via Door Locks” (confirmation with blinking lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Unlocking Confirmation (Horn) via Door Locks” (confirmation with a beep or horn)</em></p>","tiguan-5n-enable-driving-school-mode":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Adds a “Driving School” mode view to the RCD 210 / RCD 310 or the Discover MIB2 PQ, which displays turn signals, speed, and more… (Also ideal for accompanied driving) <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h4>RCD 210 / RCD 310</h4>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – At the very top of this page, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>From this drop-down menu, select “<strong>Channel 2</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu toward the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>From this menu, select “<strong>1</strong>” and then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/golf6_golf_vi_fahrschulfunktion-5b883ac1.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<h4>Discover MIB2 PQ:</h4>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule function list CAN-Driving_school</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_driving_school</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicule menu operation-menu_display_driving_school_over_threshold_high</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_6384-e21a59b4.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-folding-mirrors-with-ignition-off-and-door-open":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Allows mirrors to be folded down even after the ignition has been switched off and a door opened.  </p>\n<p><em>(Also enables windows and sunroof to be closed)</em> </p>\n<p><em>Only for Tiguan 5N phase 1.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>6</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Uncheck “Power Windows/Sunroof disabled after door Opening”.</em></p>\n<p>If coding does not work on the VCDS procedure on the VCP :</p>\n<p>For 3rd generation door modules (models up to 2011) activation is only possible with VCP Click on Guided Functions then select the “Convenience” module on the right then “Activation automatic folder mirrors in UDS door control units (Passat/ Tiguan / Jetta)”.  </p>\n<p>Setting, Command: “Folding with driver door” or “Folding with ignition” = with driver door or with key</p>\n<p>Engine/Car type : CAN TP20 1K0/5K0</p>\n<p>Start the procedure, but don’t forget to save the Conductor 42 door module with access code 04354.</p>","tiguan-5n-full-sunroof-opening-with-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows the sunroof to be opened completely when opening with the remote control. (5N and 5N2)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 (for Facelift models without the comfort module, skip directly to line 2):</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“46 – Comfort Module.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click <strong>“Encoding 07,”</strong>then click “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte<strong> 8: </strong> </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Comfort Opening Sunroof via Remote Control active” </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Uncheck “Comfort Opening Type for Sunroof (0 = open/ 1 = lift)” </em> </p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>4F – Power Plant II </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click <strong>“Encoding 07,”</strong>then click “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte<strong> 1</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0: </strong> Uncheck “Comfort function Sliding Roof: Tilted”</em></p>","tiguan-5n-headlamp-washer-duration-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to set how long the headlight washers remain activated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 04</strong> (Headlight Washer Activation Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select a duration between <strong>50 and 10,000 ms</strong> (in 50-ms increments).</p>","tiguan-5n-leaving-home-duration-setting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the length of time the headlights remain on after the car is unlocked.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10”</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 02</strong> (Leaving-Home Time)  </p>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – Select duration from <strong>0 to 60 sec</strong> (in 1sec increments).</p>","tiguan-5n-locking-the-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-the-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the RNS 510’s CD/DVD eject button.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 43</strong> (Ejection Lock)</em> then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>(CD/DVD Ejection Lock active)</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-odb-color-versions":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to select the version of your color ODB.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>”.<br/><br/>4 – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>” .<br/><br/>5 – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Display depiction</strong>”.<br/><br/>6 – On this same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this, <em>choose “Version 1, Version 2 or Version 3” </em>then confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/odb_couleur_193-1cd1bd22.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-ops-speed-camera-display-on-car-radio-screen":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the display of OPS speed cameras on the car radio screen.  </p>\n<p><strong><em>Please note: The vehicle must be equipped with a compatible car radio (RCD-310, RCD-510, RNS-315, RNS-510).</em></strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“10-Station assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding- 07</strong>”. then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Tick “Optical illustration active”.</em></p>","tiguan-5n-permanent-headlamp-deactivation-scandinavian":"<p><strong>Purpose: Allows you </strong>to disable the low beams that are always on; they are activated only when set to “Auto,” and during the day, only the parking lights are on. (Disable Scandinavian Mode)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>2007 à 2011:</em></p>\n<p>Uncheck Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>3</strong></p>\n<p><em>From 2011:</em></p>\n<p>Byte <strong>11</strong> Bit <strong>2</strong>: Uncheck “Permanent Running Light (via Low Beam) active”.  </p>","tiguan-5n-programming-a-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to program the remote controls that will be used with the vehicle for central locking and unlocking.  </p>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING:</strong> This procedure does not allow you to program the remote controls with the vehicle’s immobilizer.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01 ( </strong>“Remote Control Adaptation” from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Enter the number of keys to program, then click <strong>Save</strong>.<br/>Next, press the <strong>Unlock</strong> button on each remote control to be programmed for at least 1 second. The flashing lights will confirm the procedure.<br/>All keys must be programmed in a single session, one after the other.<br/>Programming all keys must not take longer than <strong>15 seconds</strong>.<br/>You can add up to <strong>4 remote controls</strong>. If the <strong>[Test]</strong> and/or <strong>[Save]</strong> buttons are grayed out and unclickable, the module likely has all 4 slots filled; delete the remote controls using the <strong> “Reset Remote Controls”</strong> tutorial.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel01-10148edb.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-radar-deactivation-speed-or-reversing-camera":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Selects the speed at which the reversing camera and radars are deactivated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“10 – Assistance Stationnt</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Channel 23 ( Choose the new speed, 20 km/h being the maximum )</p>","tiguan-5n-removing-the-electric-handbrake-without-braking":"<p><br/><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to remove the electric handbrake without having fastened your seatbelt, and without having your foot on the brake.  </p>\n<p><strong>This can be dangerous if you have children or pets inside</strong>.  </p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“53 – Stationnt brake</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“61378</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Choose <strong>Channel 04</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to<strong> 0</strong></em><br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/pf2-f86aa92b.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-resetting-the-remote-controls":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Resets the settings for all remote controls associated with the vehicle.</p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ WARNING:</strong> After completing this procedure, all remote controls will be deleted and will need to be reprogrammed using the <strong>“How to Program a Remote Control”</strong> tutorial <strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 00</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>0</strong> and save</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel00-caced031.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-selective-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Used to set up selective door unlocking. </p>\n<p>When unlocking the vehicle, only the driver’s door is unlocked. To unlock all doors, press the remote control’s unlock button twice.   </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>46 – Comfort Module</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p>Select <strong>Channel 03</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>If the adaptation channel is not activated.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“46 – Comfort module</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on ” <strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Selective Central Locking (Single Door Opening)” </em> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Verrouillage-automatique-des-portieres-1K0_Module4-be0b33ff.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-speed-limit-display-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to display the speed limit on the RNS 510 navigation screen.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”. Then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong><br/>Activate Bit <strong>2</strong>: Speed Threshold for Destination Input active</p>\n<p>+ use voice command to activate Bit 3: Speed Threshold for Speech Destination Input active</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510speed-9dcbaa67.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n-activate-daytime-running-lights-with-fog-lamps-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows fog lights to be used as daytime running lights.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte 0: </em><br/><em>Bit 4: Check “Daytime Running Lights (North America)”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/scandinavie_194-c7df4fa8.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7 – </strong> <em>Byte 17: </em><br/><em>Bit 4: Check “Daytime Running Light with dimmed Low Beam” (or “Daytime Running Light via Fog Lights,” depending on your version of VCDS)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/ab_975-e7b60077.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/veilleusejour3-c639151f.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>8-</strong> Adjusting the fog light intensity (from 1% to 99%)</p>\n<p><em>Byte 20: </em><br/><em>Change the value in the Dec box</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/VagComByte20-adce5646.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-activate-discover-hidden-menu":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Activates the green hidden menu (green menu, hidden menu, testmode, engineer mode) on Discover MIB2 (2014/2015).  </p>\n<p>/!\\ Caution: Making certain changes in the hidden menu may cause MIB2 to freeze or no longer start /!\\</p>\n<p><em>For model Facelift (radio screen like Golf 7).  </em><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“S12345</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Developer mode</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value<strong>“activated</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Restart MIB2, keep MENU button pressed until testmode menu appears</em><br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode-bfa51f40.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/developermode2-1024x576-7a0c833c.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-activate-off-road-mode-on-discover-pq":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add Offroad mode to Discover PQ with navigation.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Warning! There are 3 lines of coding to do here. </strong> <br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_List_BAP_Gen2-compass_0x15</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.<br/><br/><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Car_Function_Adaptations_Gen2-menu_display_Compass_over-threshold_high</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<hr/>\n<p>Restart the Discover Media PQ (hold down the ON/OFF button for at least 5 seconds).</p>\n<p>Depending on your hardware and firmware, the off-road menu may appear directly in the Menu, or it may be hidden:<br/>Press the VOICE-MENU-NAV buttons to access the secret menu, where you’ll now find the OFFROAD screen:  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadpq-1024x768-39023fd7.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroadmenupq-1024x619-dc3e8b4c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure>\n</figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/offroad-1024x631-441bee99.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-activate-reversing-camera-retrofit":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rearview camera after it has been installed on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510 or Discover MIB2 PQ (retrofit). <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h4>RCD/RNS :</h4>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>3</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>6</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) installed/active.”</p>\n<hr/>\n<h4>Discover MIB2 PQ:</h4>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select byte <strong>19</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>4</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) Low installed (PR-KA1).”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/C25A41FA-66F7-4FC9-B7F4-1761395A1D01-1024x483-11bbd3cf.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong><strong><strong>Line 2 (Optional, if parking assist is available)</strong> <strong>:</strong></strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>0</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>5</strong> to “Rear View Camera installed.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/CA86A611-2F74-4201-B791-7A74BC107A01-1024x482-c9f00e16.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><br/><strong>Hardware upgrade :</strong></p>\n<p>The camera’s video cable is connected to the infotainment control unit. It is installed in the glovebox.   <br/><br/>The two pins from the backup camera are used in the 12-pin Quadlock connector (blue).<br/><br/>Quadblock Assignment :<br/><br/>Pin 6 = video line<br/>Pin 12 = shielding</p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-corner-lights-activation":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activating the <strong>cornering lights</strong> causes the fog light on the side toward which you’re turning the steering wheel to turn on when traveling at speeds below 50 km/h. This feature is also known as “cornering lights.” Once this feature is activated on your Tiguan Facelift, the fog light on the side of the turn you’re making will turn on! It’s super handy on narrow roads or in roundabouts.     </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Control Unit</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4-Activation-des-feux-en-virage-sur-Golf-5-et-6-f4e51c90.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select  </p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Cornering Light Activation Time Limited”</em></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7: </strong> Check “Cornering Lights via Front Fog Lights active”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-255e876b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu<br/>, then click “OK.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-2a08cc40.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-adapting-brake-assist":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to configure brake assist.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>09</strong> (Brake Assist from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value</em><br/> 0<em>“medium” </em><br/>1 “low” (with low assistance, the brake pedal will be harder and more pressure will be required to brake)<br/>2 “high” (with high assistance, the brake pedal will be softer and less pressure will be required to brake)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/assistfreing6-05b83882.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-add-daytime-running-lights-drl-to-the-odb":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to enable or disable daytime running lights (DRL) in the ODB (MFA). (2011+)</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>15</strong>: Bit <strong>7</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light (DRL) Active Adaptation (MFA+)”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlmfag6-54cdc95d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlmfag62-c1d9cfb9.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-ambient-light-intensity":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Used to adjust ambient lighting intensity. And activate it for retrofit. (floor lighting)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>” then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 27</strong> (Footwell Lightning Dimming)  </p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select intensity from 20 to 100% (in 1% increments)</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>If your lighting is not activated or after retrofit installation<em>.</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” and then click on ” “.<strong><strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong></strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then on “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong>.</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>20</strong>: </em>Set <em>Bit <strong>0</strong> </em> </p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-automatic-door-locks":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to set automatic door locking from 15km/h.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Channel 04 (Auto-Lock drop-down list) <em>Set value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2 : </strong> Check “Auto-Lock active”. </em> </p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-automatic-door-unlocking":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to set automatic door unlocking when the key is removed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Channel 05 (drop-down list (Auto-Unlock)) <em>Set value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw-door-unlock-798a1163.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0 : </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Auto-Unlock active”. </em> </p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-automatically-folding-mirrors":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Automatically folds mirrors when vehicle is locked.  </p>\n<p>For 4th generation door modules (models from 2013) activation is possible with VCDS VAG-COM (Procedure with VCP for 3rd generation at bottom of page).</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>42 – Driver’s door</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“04354</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select the “<strong>System_Parameter_0-System</strong> Parameter Byte8” channel from the drop-down list.</p>\n<p>Replace Value <strong>90</strong> (if several values, the 90 is in the middle, e.g.: xxxx90xxxx )</p>\n<p>Set value according to mirror opening mode: <br/> – <strong>95</strong> (mirrors<em> will deploy when door is opened)</em><br/><em> – <strong>99</strong> (mirrors will deploy when ignition is switched on)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/DCA8744A-30AB-4C05-B633-4F3B76D90C50-4f152256.webp\"/></figure>\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>VCP</strong> (Vag Can Pro) : For 3rd generation door modules (models up to 2011) activation is only possible with VCP.</p>\n<p>Click on Guided Functions then select the “Convenience” module on the right then “Activation automatic folder mirrors in UDS door control units (Passat/ Tiguan / Jetta)”.</p>\n<p>Setting, Command: “Folding with driver door” or “Folding with ignition” = with driver door or with key</p>\n<p>Engine/Car type : CAN TP20 1K0/5K0</p>\n<p>Start the procedure, but don’t forget to save the Conductor 42 door module with access code 04354.</p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-coming-leaving-home-with-fog-lamps":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables fog lamps to be used for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte<strong> 17</strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-coming-leaving-home-with-xenons":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Activates xenon headlamps instead of fog lamps for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>17 </strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-daytime-running-lights-drl-off-with-handbrake-on":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to deactivate the daytime running lights (DRL) when the handbrake is engaged. (After the end of 2009)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: If this is a hidden bit, replace the last <strong>0</strong> on the right side of the binary number with <strong>a 1</strong>. (<strong>10001000</strong> =&gt; <strong>10001001</strong>)</em></p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-deactivate-brake-pad-warning-light":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable the brake pad wear warning light on the OBD (On-Board Diagnostics) system, for example, for brake pads without a sensor or if the sensor is malfunctioning / Brake Pad Warning Light Deactivation. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>17 – Instruments</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Cliquer sur « <strong>Codage – 07</strong> » puis cliquer sur « <strong>Assistant Codage Long</strong>« .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>: “<br/>” Then uncheck bit <strong>0: </strong> <strong>“Brakepad warning active/installed”</strong> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant-frein-d4619ec9.gif\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-deactivate-mirrorlink":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable or remove MirrorLink from App-Connect on the MIB Discover. The MirrorLink service has not been natively available on Android since June 1, 2020. For a direct connection to Android Auto.   <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Vehicle configuration-Mirror_link</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On the same page, you’ll find a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“Disabled</strong>” and confirm.</p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-deactivating-the-windshield-washer-indicator":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>2: </strong>“<strong>Washer Fluid warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglace-edc83d4f.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-beep":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: Enables </strong>confirmation of vehicle locking/unlocking via beeps (in conjunction with the alarm) and adds the beep selection menu to the ODB (MFA).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong> Select Byte <strong>5</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation via Horn Active”<br/>Bit <strong>4: </strong> Check “Unlocking Confirmation via Horn Active”</p>\n<p>To add the beep selection menu to the ODB (MFA):</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Disable “<em> </em>” “<em>Horn Confirmation Adaptation Blocked (Adaptation Channel 010/011 &amp; MFA+/FIS)</em>“</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/horng6-2ffc7685.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/horng62-14ab4a90.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-electronic-differential-lock-xds":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the electronic differential lock (XDS).  <br/><br/>The Electronic Differential Lock (XDS) is an extension of the familiar EDS function.<br/>XDS does not react to acceleration slip, however, but unloads the inside front wheel when cornering. <br/>XDS applies pressure to the inside wheel during cornering from the hydraulic ESP to prevent wheelspin.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“03 – ABS brakes</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – Select Channel<strong> 67</strong> (Electronic Differential Lock (XDS) from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Set value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-enable-usb-port-for-iphone-carplay-retrofit":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the USB port for iPhone CarPlay accounting (after activating App Connect and changing the USB and/or USB cable) for Discover MIB2 PQ (2014/2015). (Retrofit) </p>\n<p>For firmware references: <br/>MST2_EU_VW_PQ_P02XXT</p>\n<p>Modify the MIB2 coding and adaptation to recognize the new USB port (USB connector ref 5Q0 035 726 E) for both CarPlay and USB multimedia playback. A coding pin on the connector needs to be modified.  </p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"#/t/app-connect-carplay-activation\">–&gt; App Connect Activation for CarPlay and Android Auto</a><br/><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">–&gt; USB/AUX Port for VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E on VAG Custom</a></strong><br/><a href=\"#/vw/tiguan-5n/tiguan-5n2-facelift-deactivate-mirrorlink\"><strong>–&gt; Disable MirrorLink</strong></a><br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Codage- 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Assistant Codage Long</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5 </strong>– Select byte<strong>“19</strong>“<br/>Then check Bit<strong>“6-7</strong>” (C0 USB Configuration: USB and iPhone Functionality)<br/><br/><strong>Ligne 2 <strong>(optional)</strong> :</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“5F – Electr. information</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“20103</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose “<strong><strong>Interface for external media activation – connection 1</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, choose the value “<strong><strong>activated</strong></strong>“<br/><br/><br/></p>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/activation-app-connect-pour-volkswagen/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Activation APP CONNECT pour Volkswagen</a></blockquote>\n</figure>\n<figure>\n<blockquote><a href=\"https://www.vag-custom.fr/produit/prise-usb-aux-vw-golf-7-carplay-media-mib2-5q0-035-726-e/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Prise USB / AUX VW Golf 7 CarPlay Media MIB2 5Q0 035 726 E</a></blockquote>\n</figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Brake Light active” (to activate brake lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Turn Signal active” (to activate turn signals)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/emergencybreakg6-7e26fa37.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-hill-hold-control":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: Enables </strong>Hill Hold Control (Hill Start Assist).  </p>\n<p>Hill Hold Control maintains brake pressure for a few seconds after the brake pedal is held down for an extended period.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>“</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Hill Hold Control (HHC/PR-UG1/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: Hill Hold Control Settings.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p>Select <strong>Channel 58</strong> (Hill Hold Control (HHC) from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Select a value:<br/>0 “normal”<br/>1 “earlier” (restarts with lower acceleration)<br/>2 “later” (restarts with higher acceleration)</p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-mute-push-to-talk-button":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to reconfigure the Push-To-Talk (PTT) button at the bottom left of your multifunction steering wheel to function as a mute button for the audio volume. (2010 and later)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>16 – Multifunction Steering Wheel.”</strong><br/></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding- 07</strong>”. then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 1</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck </em><em>“Multi-Function-Steering-Wheel (MFSW) with Push-To-Talk (PPT) Button installed</em>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/pttg6-da3300eb.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>The Push-to-Talk (PPT) button now acts as a mute button.</p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-needle-check":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> activates needle sweep when the car is started. (Needle Sweep)   </p>\n<p><em>Information </em>: If your meter is not compatible, the channel is inactive.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>” then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu to choose a channel and select the “<strong>Staging</strong>” channel, if unavailable select the “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” channel:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg6-9456b738.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the “<strong>New value</strong>” box, click on the drop-down menu and select “<strong>active</strong>”. Once this new value has been entered, click on “<strong>Save</strong>”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg62-c8918051.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-programming-a-remote-control":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to program the remote controls that will be used with the vehicle for central locking and unlocking.  </p>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING:</strong> This procedure does not allow you to program remote controls with the vehicle’s immobilizer.<br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Ignition Authorization)</strong>, you cannot program a new remote control using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01 ( </strong>“Remote Control Adaptation” from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Enter the number of keys to program, then click <strong>Save</strong>.<br/>Next, press the <strong>Unlock</strong> button on each remote control to be programmed for at least 1 second. The flashing lights will confirm the process.<br/>All keys must be programmed in a single session, one after the other.<br/>Programming all keys must not take longer than <strong>15 seconds</strong>.<br/>You can add up to <strong>7 remote controls</strong>. If the <strong>[Test]</strong> and/or <strong>[Save]</strong> buttons are grayed out and unclickable, the module likely has all 7 slots filled; delete the remote controls using the <strong>“Reset Remote Controls”</strong> tutorial.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/programmertelecommande-51bf4068.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-remove-alarm-belt":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>1: </strong>“<strong>Seatbelt warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-resetting-the-remote-controls":"<figure><img alt=\"VAG Coding VCDS ODBeleven VW Tiguan 5N2 facelift\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Resets the settings for all remote controls associated with the vehicle. </p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ WARNING:</strong> After completing this procedure, all remote controls will be deleted and will need to be reprogrammed using the <strong>“Program a Remote Control”</strong> tutorial <strong>.</strong><br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Start Authorization)</strong>, you cannot delete the remote controls using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 00</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>0</strong> and save</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel00-caced031.webp\"/></figure>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-selective-door-unlocking":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to configure selective door unlocking.  </p>\n<p>When unlocking the vehicle, only the driver’s door is unlocked. To unlock all doors, press the remote control’s unlock button twice.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Channel 03 (drop-down list: Selective (Single) Door Locking) <em>Set the value to 1</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 3: </strong> Check “Selective Central Locking active (Single Door Locking)” </em> </p>","tiguan-5n2-facelift-start-stop-deactivation":"<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_tiguan_5n_facelift-a0cf68c0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the Start/Stop function completely.  <br/><br/><br/><strong><em>Only compatible with Gateway 7N0! Temperature deactivation method. </em></strong> <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Long Adaptation – 0A”</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Channel<strong>“13</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – In new value, select<strong>“D02000</strong>” (default value = <strong>002000</strong>) then validate.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/gof6startstop-1024x528-699ec970.webp\"/></figure>"};
